{'symbol': 'ILMN', 'date': '2023-01-09 06:00:00', 'title': 'GRAIL INTRODUCES STATE-OF-THE-ART METHYLATION-BASED SOLUTION TO ACCELERATE CANCER RESEARCH IN THE POST-DIAGNOSIS SETTING', 'text': "MENLO PARK, CALIF.--( BUSINESS WIRE )--GRAIL, LLC, A HEALTHCARE COMPANY WHOSE MISSION IS TO DETECT CANCER EARLY WHEN IT CAN BE CURED, TODAY ANNOUNCED THE AVAILABILITY OF A STATE-OF-THE-ART RESEARCH USE ONLY OFFERING FOR BIOPHARMACEUTICAL COMPANIES. THE NEW TECHNOLOGY SOLUTION USES GRAIL'S PROPRIETARY TARGETED METHYLATION PLATFORM TO ANALYZE CELL-FREE DNA (CFDNA) ISOLATED FROM PERIPHERAL BLOOD FOR CANCER SIGNAL INTERROGATION. POTENTIAL RESEARCH USE CASES INCLUDE, BUT ARE NOT LIMITED TO, PROGNOSIS, MINIMAL RESIDUAL DISEASE DETECTION, AND RECURRENCE MONITORING ACROSS DIFFERENT CANCER TYPES IN RESEARCH STUDIES."}